With agent exclusions, you can prevent agents from receiving software updates at specified times.
Use the API to perform a standard set of CRUD operations on agent exclusion objects.
For background information about agent exclusions, also known as freeze windows, see Freeze
Windows in the Tenable Vulnerability Management User Guide.
{
"auto_unlink":
-
{
"enabled": "false",
"expiration": 30
},
"concurrent_update":
-
{
"enabled": "true",
"max_concurrent_update": 500
},
"software_update": "true",
"hybrid_scanning_enabled": false
}
